{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-316298",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{6}{\\pi }(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }[(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}))-(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\cdot 0)+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }[(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(0+0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }[(\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1)-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }(\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{16}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
